# Privacy Policy for LinkDeed

**Last Updated:** March 29, 2026

## 1. Introduction

Welcome to LinkDeed. This Privacy Policy explains how LinkDeed (“we”, “our”, or “us”) collects, uses, stores, and protects your information when you use the LinkDeed AI Job Automation App and website (the “Service”). By using LinkDeed, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy.

## 2. Information We Collect

We may collect the following types of information:

### Personal Information

When you register or use LinkDeed, we may collect:

* Full name
* Email address
* Phone number
* Location
* Resume/CV information
* Job preferences
* LinkedIn profile information (if connected)

### Account & Usage Information

We may collect:

* Jobs you search for
* Jobs you apply to
* Application activity
* Login activity
* Device information
* IP address
* Browser type

### Payment Information

If you subscribe to paid services, we may collect payment details through secure third-party payment processors. We do not store your full card details on our servers.

## 3. How We Use Your Information

We use your information to:

* Create and manage your account
* Automatically search for relevant jobs
* Automatically apply to jobs on your behalf
* Send job alerts and notifications
* Improve our AI job matching system
* Provide customer support
* Process payments
* Prevent fraud and abuse
* Improve our platform and user experience

## 4. Automatic Job Applications

By using LinkDeed, you authorize us to use your provided information (including your CV, profile details, and job preferences) to automatically apply to jobs on your behalf through supported job platforms.

## 5. Sharing Your Information

We do not sell your personal information. We may share your information with:

* Job platforms and recruiters when applying for jobs
* Payment processors for subscription payments
* Cloud storage providers
* Analytics providers
* Legal authorities if required by law

## 6. Data Storage and Security

We store your data on secure servers and implement reasonable security measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, loss, misuse, or alteration. However, no system is 100% secure.

## 7. Your Rights

You have the right to:

* Access your personal data
* Update or correct your information
* Delete your account and data
* Stop automatic job applications
* Unsubscribe from emails

To request data deletion, contact us at: **[support@linkdeed.pro](mailto:support@linkdeed.pro)**

## 8. Data Retention

We keep your information for as long as your account is active or as needed to provide services. If you delete your account, we will delete your personal data within a reasonable time unless required by law to keep it.

## 9. Cookies and Tracking

We may use cookies and similar tracking technologies to:

* Keep you logged in
* Understand user behavior
* Improve our services
* Analyze traffic and usage

You can disable cookies in your browser settings.

## 10. Third-Party Links

LinkDeed may contain links to third-party job websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those websites.

## 11. Children's Privacy

LinkDeed is not intended for individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.

## 12. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we update it, we will revise the “Last Updated” date.

